From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:41:25 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Plutonium: what the user starts comes to the front; a
 toast for the rest

Windows from a terminal the user types in, or from the app launcher, open
in their thread's panel with the keyboard (in another thread, they wait in
its panel and a toast offers them). Terminals get the helper's terminalEnv
(PLUTONIUM_SHOW); setup and settle scripts, which run by themselves, don't.
What an agent opens waits in its thread, with a toast while that thread is
open. Windows and tabs that close within a second get none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
